<article class="env-lemma" id="0DEX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DEX">Lemma <span data-tag="0DEX">59.101.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. For $\mathcal{F}$ a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ S$-module on $S_{\acute{e}tale}$ the maps </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \pi _ S^*\mathcal{F} \longrightarrow R\epsilon _{S, *}(a_ S^*\mathcal{F}) \quad \text{and}\quad \mathcal{F} \longrightarrow Ra_{S, *}(a_ S^*\mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> are isomorphisms with $a_ S : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits ((\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (S_{\acute{e}tale})$ as above. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is an immediate consequence of parts (6) and (7) of Lemma <a href="/tag/0DEW" data-tag="0DEW">59.101.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>